		skos:definition	"This industry includes companies that purchase network capacity and/or facilities on a wholesale basis from network operators and resell wired and wireless telecom services (except satellite) to businesses and households. Such companies are often referred to as resellers, because they do not operate network facilities and infrastructure. Instead, they market and resell services using other carriers' networks. Mobile virtual network operators (MVNOs) and carriers that sell prepaid calling cards are good examples of resellers."@en ;
		skos:notation	"101111" ;
		skos:prefLabel	"Telecom Resellers"@en ;
		tempo:validFrom	"2014-08-08"^^xsd:date ;
