		pav:sourceLastAccessedOn	"2019-12-03T20:05:01Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
		skos:definition	"This segment includes companies that manufacture pacemakers. These devices deliver electrical impulses to correct abnormally slow heart rhythms (arrhythmias). The device is composed of two pieces: the can, which generates the electrical pulses, and the leads which deliver the pulses to the heart. These devices are implanted under the skin near the heart with the leads placed in the chambers of the heart. Newer generations of pacemakers are considered MRI-safe. An example of such a device is the Revo pacemaker manufactured by Medtronic (MDT US)."@en ;
		skos:notation	"15121210101014" ;
		skos:prefLabel	"Pacemakers"@en ;
		tempo:validFrom	"2014-08-08"^^xsd:date ;
